SBE1V1K board support for the QSDK 6.6 device tree.

Adds the parts of the board this project depends on and reads at runtime:

  * pwm-fan on SoC PWM channel 3 with cooling-levels <36 72 128 255>, bound to
    the top-glue-thermal zone (tsens 15) at 40/50/65/80 C. sbegw's fan policy
    reads these values rather than inventing its own; see gateway/sbegw/hwd.py.
  * Thermal zones and trip points for the CPU cluster, NSS, UBI and WCSS.
  * Port wiring: eth0/eth1 QCA8075 1G, eth2 QCA8081 2.5G, eth3 RTL8261N 10G.

The tri-colour status LED (gpio-leds red/green/blue on GPIOs 44/45/56) is
already in the base device tree and is NOT part of this patch; sbegw's LED
policy just drives it.

Apply against qca/src/linux-6.6 in a QSDK tree:

    cd qca/src/linux-6.6
    patch -p1 < .../patches/0001-ipq9570-sbe1v1k-board.patch

The base file is Qualcomm's; only the diff is distributed here.
